# The Weaver's Gift

Long ago, when the sky was empty and black, there lived a lonely weaver named Sala who crafted the most beautiful cloth in all the land. Each night, she would sit at her loom and weep, for though her work brought joy to others, she had no one to share her own heart with.

The Moon, watching from his perch above, took pity on her. He descended one evening and asked, "Why do you weep, skilled weaver?"

"I create beauty," Sala replied, "but when darkness falls, no one can see it. My work disappears into the night, like tears into an ocean."

