In ancient times, the world knew only silence and shadow. Birds existed but could not sing, and flowers bloomed without color or scent.

A young shepherd named Aria discovered an injured sparrow with wings as gray as stone. Rather than abandon it, she carried the bird home, sharing her meager bread and warming it by her fire. For seven nights, she sang lullabies to ease its pain.

On the eighth dawn, the sparrow transformed into a radiant spirit. "You gave voice to comfort me," it said. "Now I shall give voice to the world."

